| Prerequisite | Status | Blocks I0 doc? | Blocks I1 code? |
| ------------ | ------ | -------------- | --------------- |
| Phase G modular codegen on `DEV` | ✅ | No | No |
| Phase H certification (H0–H4) on `DEV` | ✅ | No | No |
| `pnpm run phase-g-h:fast-track` green | ✅ | No | No |
| G+H+I merge PR → `main` | ✅ merged [#19](https://github.com/hrokhbakhsh1991/docs/pull/19) | — | — |
| `ci:integrity` full gate | ⏳ deferred | No | Architect YES only |
| Phase I0–I2 on `DEV` | ✅ | — | — |

**Answer:** Phase I **I0–I2 are closed on `DEV`**. PR [#19](https://github.com/hrokhbakhsh1991/docs/pull/19) to `main` is open. I3 optional — Architect YES only.

## Problem

| Symptom | Risk at scale |
| ------- | ------------- |
| `importAdminThemeForPlugin` / guest theme loaders use per-plugin dynamic `import()` with no budget | Cold-start latency, unbounded parallel CSS fetches on tenant switch |
| `loadWorkspacePluginByIdFromRegistry` has in-memory `Map` cache but no TTL/size policy documented | Memory growth in long-lived dev servers; unclear prod behavior across workers |
| Plugin loaders generated file still **static-imports all sync plugins** at module init | Every workspace bundle pays parse cost even when tenant uses one `pluginId` |
| No guard tying theme import count to active `pluginId` | Regression when new workspaces add skins |

Tenant **registry** cache (API `tenant-registry-cache.ts`, DEC-068/074) is **out of scope** for Phase I — already implemented. Phase I targets **frontend generated registry** + **theme CSS ingress**.

## Non-goals (Phase I)

- Changing `workspace.manifest.json` schema or certification (`productionTier`)
- Redis / multi-replica invalidation for API tenant cache (future platform ops)
- Full `ci:integrity` as Phase I exit gate
- Removing sync plugin imports entirely (I2 may narrow, not rewrite plugin host)
- Member portal preset manifest-only admission (Phase B / G adjacency)

## Two workstreams

```text
apps/*/layout.tsx
    → importAdminThemeForPlugin(pluginId)     ← I1 theme budget
    → importGuest*ThemeForPlugin(pluginId)

apps/web bootstrap
    → loadWorkspacePluginByIdFromRegistry()  ← I2 loader cache
    → workspace-plugin-loaders.generated.ts (sync + dynamic)
```

| Stream | Source | Generated consumer | Success metric |
| ------ | ------ | ------------------ | -------------- |
| **I1 Theme import budget** | `themeStylesheets` / `guestThemeStylesheets` in manifest | `workspace-*-theme-stylesheets.generated.ts` | Admin ≤1, guest ≤2 dynamic imports per path; guard PASS |
| **I2 Registry load cache** | `workspace-plugin-loaders.generated.ts` | `loadWorkspacePluginByIdFromRegistry` | Documented TTL/size; dev HMR safe; prod single-flight |

## I1 — Theme import performance budget (target)

### Normative budget

| Surface | App | Max dynamic CSS imports per request | Notes |
| ------- | --- | ----------------------------------- | ----- |
| Admin | `apps/web` | **1** per `importAdminThemeForPlugin` call | Switch-only; no platform base skin |
| Marketing | `apps/marketing` | **2** | Phase D.3: starter base + 1 plugin overlay |
| Portal | `apps/portal` | **2** | Phase D.2: starter base + 1 plugin overlay |

**Rules:**

1. Layouts must not import more than one workspace skin CSS chain per resolved `pluginId`.
2. Generated loaders must not `import()` inactive plugins' theme files (switch-only).
3. Guard `guard:theme-import-budget` (I1) — bundles `guard-portal-guest-theme-loader`, `guard-marketing-guest-theme-loader`, admin layout checks, and per-loader `await import()` budget counts.

### Enforcement (I1)

| Check | Rule |
| ----- | ---- |
| Layouts | Exactly one `await import*ThemeForPlugin(...)` per root layout |
| Generated loaders | No top-level eager `@app-tour/workspace-*` CSS imports |
| `importAdminThemeForPlugin` | ≤1 `await import()` per execution path (switch-only) |
| `importGuest*ThemeForPlugin` | ≤2 `await import()` per path (starter base + plugin overlay) |
| CI | `pnpm run guard:theme-import-budget` in `phase-10:guard` + `phase-10-guard.yml` |

### Baseline (trunk today)

- `importAdminThemeForPlugin` — switch on 4 plugins; one dynamic import per call ✅ pattern correct, no budget guard yet.
- Guest marketing/portal — same pattern via `workspace-guest-theme-stylesheets.generated.ts`.

## I2 — Generated registry cache strategy (target)

### Current behavior

```typescript
// workspace-plugin-loaders.generated.ts (excerpt)
const pluginLoadCache = new Map<string, Promise<WorkspacePlugin>>();
```

- **Per-process** memoization of dynamic import promise — good for single-flight.
- **Sync** `SYNC_WORKSPACE_PLUGINS` eagerly constructs all trunk plugins at module load — scales O(workspaces) at boot. **Removed in P4.1 / I3** — web loaders are async-only (`loadWorkspacePluginByIdFromRegistry`).

### Target policy (I2)

| Env | Policy |
| --- | ------ |
| **Production** | Promise cache via `workspace-plugin-load-cache.ts`; max entries = **product** trunk `pluginId` count (excludes `registryOnly` finance/booking fixtures); key = `pluginId` only (no tenant bleed) |
| **Dev (Next HMR)** | Cache bust when `WORKSPACE_PLUGIN_REGISTRY_REVISION` changes (codegen regen) or via `invalidateWorkspacePluginLoadCache()` |
| **Codegen** | `generateWebLoaders` emits dynamic `import()` switch only — **no** top-level `@app-tour/workspace-*` static imports and **no** `SYNC_WORKSPACE_PLUGINS` (I3 / P4.1) |

**Invariant:** Phase G per-domain `--check` unchanged; I2 must not edit generated loaders by hand.

### Enforcement (I2)

| Check | Rule |
| ----- | ---- |
| Generated loaders | Must use `getOrCreateWorkspacePluginLoad` — no inline `pluginLoadCache` Map |
| Max entries | `WORKSPACE_PLUGIN_LOAD_CACHE_MAX_ENTRIES` === **product** manifest `pluginId` count |
| Revision | `WORKSPACE_PLUGIN_REGISTRY_REVISION` = sorted **product** trunk plugin ids (comma-joined) |
| No static fan-in | Generated loaders must not `import … from "@app-cloud/workspace-…"` at top level; must not define `SYNC_WORKSPACE_PLUGINS` |
| Invalidation | `invalidateWorkspacePluginLoadCache()` exported from generated bootstrap |
| CI | `pnpm run guard:workspace-plugin-load-cache` in `phase-10:guard` + `phase-i:fast-track` + `phase-10-guard.yml` |
| Cold-path fan-in budget (P4-D2) | `pnpm run guard:p4-cold-path-fan-in` — numeric report `reports/p4-cold-path-fan-in.json`; see [`p4-d2-cold-path-fan-in-ci.mdoc`](./p4-d2-cold-path-fan-in-ci.mdoc) |

